id: temporal/grammar/0167
area: temporal
op: Temporal.PlainYearMonth.from (string), toString
in: str:"1900-02-29"
out: error: RangeError
class: divergence
divergence.broiler-js: row G3: a year-month string's day is captured and validated only outside ISO 8601 and the Gregorian family, so a year-month whose day is not a date (2020-02-30, 2020-01-00, 2021-02-29) is read as its year-month, where DateSpec's early error makes it a RangeError; correction (a lenient grammar acceptance), answered by SJL-10.5
prov: proposal:temporal@e8cc03fc#sec-temporal-iso8601grammar proposal:temporal@e8cc03fc#sec-temporal-parseisodatetime proposal:temporal@e8cc03fc#sec-temporal.plainyearmonth.from ref:temporalref@1
script: Temporal.PlainYearMonth.from("1900-02-29").toString()
