id: temporal/grammar/0318
area: temporal
op: Temporal.PlainTime.from (string), toString
in: str:"\u0661\u0662:\u0663\u0660"
out: error: RangeError
class: divergence
divergence.broiler-js: row G9: digits are matched with .NET's \d, which admits every Unicode decimal digit, and int.Parse then lets a FormatException escape the evaluation (in the four plain types' offset the digits are accepted and the offset ignored), where the grammar's DecimalDigit is ASCII and the string a RangeError; correction (a lenient grammar acceptance), answered by SJL-10.5
prov: proposal:temporal@e8cc03fc#sec-temporal-iso8601grammar proposal:temporal@e8cc03fc#sec-temporal-parseisodatetime proposal:temporal@e8cc03fc#sec-temporal.plaintime.from ref:temporalref@1
script: Temporal.PlainTime.from("\u0661\u0662:\u0663\u0660").toString()
note: rows G5 and G7: a time alone (TimeSpec, and the early errors of a designator-less time that is also a month-day or year-month); decimal digits other than ASCII (row G9)
since: 24

id: temporal/grammar/0319
area: temporal
op: Temporal.PlainTime.from (string), toString
in: str:"12:30:45.\u0661"
out: error: RangeError
class: divergence
divergence.broiler-js: row G9: digits are matched with .NET's \d, which admits every Unicode decimal digit, and int.Parse then lets a FormatException escape the evaluation (in the four plain types' offset the digits are accepted and the offset ignored), where the grammar's DecimalDigit is ASCII and the string a RangeError; correction (a lenient grammar acceptance), answered by SJL-10.5
prov: proposal:temporal@e8cc03fc#sec-temporal-iso8601grammar proposal:temporal@e8cc03fc#sec-temporal-parseisodatetime proposal:temporal@e8cc03fc#sec-temporal.plaintime.from ref:temporalref@1
