id: temporal/grammar/0728
area: temporal
op: Temporal.PlainDate.from (string), toString
in: str:"2020-01-01T12:00+\u0660\u0661:\u0660\u0660"
out: error: RangeError
class: divergence
divergence.broiler-js: row G9: digits are matched with .NET's \d, which admits every Unicode decimal digit, and int.Parse then lets a FormatException escape the evaluation (in the four plain types' offset the digits are accepted and the offset ignored), where the grammar's DecimalDigit is ASCII and the string a RangeError; correction (a lenient grammar acceptance), answered by SJL-10.5
prov: proposal:temporal@e8cc03fc#sec-temporal-iso8601grammar proposal:temporal@e8cc03fc#sec-temporal-parseisodatetime proposal:temporal@e8cc03fc#sec-temporal.plaindate.from ref:temporalref@1
