id: temporal/grammar/1445
area: temporal
op: Temporal.Duration.from (string), toString
in: str:"P\u0661D"
out: error: RangeError
class: divergence
divergence.broiler-js: row G9: digits are matched with .NET's \d, which admits every Unicode decimal digit, and int.Parse then lets a FormatException escape the evaluation (in the four plain types' offset the digits are accepted and the offset ignored), where the grammar's DecimalDigit is ASCII and the string a RangeError; correction (a lenient grammar acceptance), answered by SJL-10.5
prov: proposal:temporal@e8cc03fc#sec-temporal-parsetemporaldurationstring proposal:temporal@e8cc03fc#sec-temporal.duration.from ref:temporalref@1
script: Temporal.Duration.from("P\u0661D").toString()
note: rows G21 to G23: duration strings (designators, part order, a fraction on the last time part, a time designator with a part, signs, each field at and past its limit); decimal digits other than ASCII (row G9)
since: 24

