id: temporal/grammar/1559
area: temporal
op: ToTemporalCalendarIdentifier (string), a property bag's calendar
in: str:"1214[u-ca=gregory]"
out: error: RangeError
class: divergence
divergence.broiler-js: row G17: a calendar string is read by TemporalIsoString.TryParse, which refuses none of the strings ParseTemporalCalendarString refuses (a time with Z, a year-month or month-day with a calendar, an empty, unknown critical or misplaced annotation, an offset out of range) and of several u-ca annotations answers the last, where the first rules; correction (a lenient grammar acceptance), answered by SJL-10.5
prov: proposal:temporal@e8cc03fc#sec-temporal-parsetemporalcalendarstring proposal:temporal@e8cc03fc#sec-temporal-parseisodatetime proposal:temporal@e8cc03fc#sec-temporal-totemporalcalendaridentifier overruled:temporalref@1=value:str:"gregory"
script: Temporal.PlainDate.from({year: 2020, monthCode: "M01", day: 1, calendar: "1214[u-ca=gregory]"}).calendarId
note: rows G17 and C2: a calendar string (ParseTemporalCalendarString; of several u-ca annotations, the first); decision D7: the pinned text's answer, where its polyfill answers str:"gregory": the string parses only as a year-month or month-day, for which ParseISODateTime throws with a calendar other than iso8601, and it is no AnnotationValue, so ParseTemporalCalendarString throws a RangeError
since: 24

